usage: c1-run.py [-h] [--lane-root LANE_ROOT] [--carriers CARRIERS]
                 [--evidence-root EVIDENCE_ROOT] [--scratch SCRATCH]
                 [--carrier CARRIER] [--include-exploratory]
                 [--timeout TIMEOUT] [--freeze FREEZE] [--dry-run]
                 [--data-run] [--keep-scratch] [--force] [--no-unblob-log-tee]
                 [--rea-outdir-mode {scratch,evidence}] [--fake-rea FAKE_REA]

kaidoku round 49 R49-C1 after-freeze data procedure.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --lane-root LANE_ROOT
                        lane root (default: nearest ancestor with
                        corpus/evidence and plans/)
  --carriers CARRIERS   carriers.json (default:
                        <lane>/tools/round-49/carriers.json)
  --evidence-root EVIDENCE_ROOT
                        evidence root (default:
                        <lane>/corpus/evidence/round-49/c1)
  --scratch SCRATCH     scratch base (default: $HYAKU_SCRATCH or
                        /fast/scratch/hyaku; the runner appends /kaidoku-r49)
  --carrier CARRIER     run only this carrier id (repeatable)
  --include-exploratory
                        also run carriers.json ids listed under
                        scope.exploratory_ids (the claim does not score them)
  --timeout TIMEOUT     per-carrier REA timeout in seconds (default 900)
  --freeze FREEZE       freeze revision recorded in the receipts
  --dry-run             print the commands that would run; write nothing
  --data-run            assert that the freeze is in place (required to write
                        into the default evidence root)
  --keep-scratch        keep the per-carrier scratch directory
  --force               replace an existing evidence directory (REA refuses an
                        existing output root, so a re-run must replace it)
  --no-unblob-log-tee   run unblob directly (no log tee): the extract command
                        line is then not captured
  --rea-outdir-mode {scratch,evidence}
                        where REA's output_directory points (default scratch =
                        this round's /kaidoku-r49/ scratch segment, the
                        binding the frozen claims text states: the produced
                        tree is copied verbatim into the evidence dir and
                        provenance.json binds the two; evidence = REA writes
                        into the evidence dir itself, so the receipt names
                        that path)
  --fake-rea FAKE_REA   DEVELOPMENT ONLY: replace the REA command with this
                        argv prefix (a stand-in that prints a synthetic
                        envelope). The receipt records the override, and a
                        synthetic receipt fails the counter's evidence-id and
                        rerun-projection bindings.
